---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Programmes — Virtue Literacy Africa"
  description="VLA's five programme pillars: literacy programmes, mobile and community learning, innovation and AI in education including Mwangaza AI, community partnerships, and research and evidence."
  currentPage="/programmes"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Programmes</span>
      <h1>Five pillars. One ecosystem.</h1>
      <p>Each pillar answers a different part of the same problem: children whose communities move, or have been moved, and whose schooling was designed on the assumption that they would not.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLAR 1 — LITERACY PROGRAMMES -->
  <section class="pillar-section" id="literacy">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ps-head reveal">
        <span class="ps-num">01</span>
        <h2>Literacy Programmes</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-intro reveal">Community-based literacy initiatives designed for children and youth, meeting them in the environments they actually live in, including mobile and seasonal communities.</p>

      <ul class="pillar-bullets reveal">
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Reading and foundational literacy sessions held where children already gather, including homes, places of worship, and shared community space.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Delivery scheduled around herding, market, and migration calendars rather than a fixed school term.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Facilitators recruited from the communities themselves, so a programme does not leave when a visitor does.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Materials in the languages children speak at home, alongside the language of instruction.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Progress tracked per child rather than per class, because attendance is not continuous.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLAR 2 — MOBILE & COMMUNITY LEARNING -->
  <section class="pillar-section" id="mobile-learning">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ps-head reveal">
        <span class="ps-num">02</span>
        <h2>Mobile &amp; Community Learning</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-intro reveal">Flexible, community-anchored learning spaces that adapt to migration, displacement, and the realities of life in arid and semi-arid areas.</p>

      <ul class="pillar-bullets reveal">
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Learning spaces that can be set up, moved, and re-established as families move.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Community reading spaces hosted by partner institutions, so a place to read outlasts any single visit.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Provision that continues through drought and displacement rather than pausing until conditions improve.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Reading materials chosen to survive the distances and conditions they travel through.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Sessions open to any child in the community, whether or not they are enrolled in a school.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLAR 3 — INNOVATION & AI, INCLUDING MWANGAZA -->
  <section class="pillar-section" id="innovation">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ps-head reveal">
        <span class="ps-num">03</span>
        <h2>Innovation &amp; AI in Education</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-intro reveal">Exploring how artificial intelligence and emerging tools can expand access to learning and equip young people with skills for the future.</p>

      <div class="ps-grid reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>Mwangaza AI &mdash; early developmental screening</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.7">Undetected developmental delays and disabilities are a significant, often invisible barrier to literacy. Children who cannot hear, see, or process language are frequently mistaken for slow learners rather than identified and supported.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.7;margin-top:1rem">This barrier compounds further in pastoralist, arid, and semi-arid communities, where specialists and screening services are often entirely out of reach, meaning these children may otherwise never be identified at all. Through Mwangaza AI, we extend early developmental screening to close that gap, identifying barriers before they compound into literacy failure and connecting children to appropriate support pathways where available.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>How it works in practice</h3>
          <ul class="pillar-bullets">
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Built to run offline on low-cost devices, for communities with little or no connectivity.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Administered by trained community facilitators and caregivers, not by a specialist who has to be present.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Screens for hearing, vision, and language-processing barriers that routinely go unnoticed.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Refers children onward to appropriate support pathways where those pathways exist.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Localisable to the languages spoken in the communities we serve.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Free at the point of use.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout reveal">
        <span class="callout-label">The Mwangaza Promise</span>
        <h3>Mwangaza will never be paywalled.</h3>
        <p><em>Mwangaza</em> means "light" in Swahili. It is built for the families who need it most, which means it has to work offline, in local languages, on the devices those families already own.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLAR 4 — COMMUNITY PARTNERSHIPS -->
  <section class="pillar-section" id="partnerships">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ps-head reveal">
        <span class="ps-num">04</span>
        <h2>Community Partnerships</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-intro reveal">Working closely with families, local leaders, and trusted institutions like churches to build sustainable, culturally grounded pathways to literacy.</p>

      <ul class="pillar-bullets reveal">
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Religious institutions, which already hold both trust and physical space in the communities we serve.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Families and caregivers, who are the most consistent teachers a mobile child has.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Local leaders, who determine whether a programme is welcome and whether it lasts.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Schools and health providers, where they are present, so a screening referral has somewhere to go.</span></li>
        <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>County and national education authorities, so that what works can outlive our involvement in it.</span></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout reveal">
        <span class="callout-label">How we enter a community</span>
        <h3>We build on existing trust rather than starting from scratch.</h3>
        <p>The communities we work in have adapted to change for generations. Our job is to add literacy provision to structures that already function, not to replace them with something that arrives and then leaves.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLAR 5 — RESEARCH & EVIDENCE -->
  <section class="pillar-section pillar-section--research" id="research">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ps-head reveal">
        <span class="ps-num">05</span>
        <h2>Research &amp; Evidence on Inclusive Education, Governance and AI</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-intro reveal">We document and publish findings from our own programmes and partnerships, generating credible evidence on what works in literacy, inclusive education, and AI-enabled learning for underprivileged and displaced children.</p>

      <div class="ps-grid reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>What we publish</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.7">Standalone reports, briefs, and case studies drawn from the programmes we run. No issues, no volumes, no subscription. Each output is written to be read by someone with a decision to make and limited time in which to make it.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.7;margin-top:1rem">Keeping the format light is deliberate. Evidence that takes a year to reach print is evidence that arrives after the decision it was meant to inform.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Who it reaches</h3>
          <ul class="pillar-bullets">
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Educators and facilitators working with mobile and displaced learners.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>County and national policymakers responsible for education provision.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Development partners deciding where funding goes and what it should buy.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pb-marker">/</span><span>Organisations running comparable programmes elsewhere on the continent.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pillar-actions reveal">
        <a href="/research" class="btn btn-coral">Research &amp; findings &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/get-involved" class="btn">Partner on research</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="act">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Support a pillar.</h2>
      <div class="act-grid reveal">
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Sponsor</h3>
          <p>Fund a literacy programme cycle, a community reading space, or a round of developmental screening. Every gift ties to a named deliverable.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/donate">See giving options &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Partner</h3>
          <p>Faith institutions, schools, NGOs, government agencies, and development partners can partner at the pillar level.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/get-involved">Start a conversation &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Volunteer your skills</h3>
          <p>Teachers, facilitators, translators, screening and disability specialists, and researchers are all welcome.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/get-involved">Get involved &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
